---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import headshot from '../assets/headshot.jpg';
import { CALENDAR_URL, EMAIL_URL } from '../data/links';
---

<Layout
  title="John Morgan"
  description="Fractional CTO for founder-led software teams. I help small engineering teams become AI-native teams that ship."
>
  <SiteHeader active="home" />

  <main>
    <section id="intro">
      <Image
        src={headshot}
        alt="John Morgan"
        class="headshot"
        width={112}
        height={112}
        densities={[1, 2]}
        loading="eager"
      />
      <h1>Fractional CTO for founder-led software teams</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        I help small engineering teams become AI-native teams that ship, and I build the
        engineering org around them as the company grows.
      </p>
      <p>
        At ManageXR I took engineering from 3 to 15 engineers as Head of Engineering while ARR
        grew 30x. Along the way I made it an AI-native team, defined how we hired and shipped, and
        stayed hands-on in the code. Before that I spent four years on Google Search Ranking as a
        Senior Software Engineer and Tech Lead.
      </p>
      <p>
        Now I work with founders part-time, as a fractional CTO or advisor, on the problems that
        show up between "a few engineers" and "a real engineering org."
      </p>
      <a class="cta" href={CALENDAR_URL}>Book a 30-minute intro call &rarr;</a>
      <p class="cta-alt"><a href={EMAIL_URL}>or email me</a></p>

      <ul class="proof-strip">
        <li><strong>3 &rarr; 15</strong> engineers built and led</li>
        <li><strong>30x</strong> ARR growth as Head of Engineering</li>
        <li><strong>Ex-Google</strong> Senior SWE / Tech Lead, Search Ranking</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="philosophy">
      <span class="eyebrow">Philosophy</span>
      <h2>How I think about engineering</h2>
      <p>
        Excellent engineering depends on excellent communication. I write things down, make sure
        the reasons behind decisions are documented, and care more about building the right thing
        than the most complex one.
      </p>
      <p>
        The best engineers are the ones who learn fastest, so I care about tight feedback loops
        and getting the most out of every attempt. That includes AI-native engineering, which I
        pushed for across ManageXR.
      </p>
      <p class="read-more"><a href="/philosophy">Read the full philosophy &rarr;</a></p>
    </section>

    <section id="experience">
      <span class="eyebrow">Experience</span>
      <h2>Work &amp; education</h2>

      <div class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h3>ManageXR · Head of Engineering</h3>
          <span class="entry-meta">Oct 2021 – May 2026</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Grew the team from 3 to 15 engineers while ARR grew 30x. Owned architecture, hiring,
          and engineering standards, led the shift to AI-native development, and stayed hands-on
          in backend and Android. Also led security and compliance for the company (SOC 2 Type II,
          ISO 27001) and worked with enterprise customers and partners during sales.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h3>Google · Senior Software Engineer, Tech Lead</h3>
          <span class="entry-meta">2017 – 2021</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Led technical direction for a critical Search Ranking backend component and reduced
          recall loss by more than 10% with large-scale ETL and feature engineering. Redesigned the
          deep neural network in the serving path, cutting tail latency by 15ms. Built the testing
          infrastructure for a major infrastructure redesign.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h3>Stanford University · B.S. Computer Science</h3>
          <span class="entry-meta">Class of 2017</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Human-Computer Interaction track. 1st place, CS Department Software Fair, for disaster
          response software. Debate Society captain, 2014–2016.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="read-more"><a href="/experience">See full experience and projects &rarr;</a></p>
    </section>

    <section id="consulting">
      <span class="eyebrow">Work with me</span>
      <h2>Fractional CTO &amp; advisory</h2>
      <p>
        I work with founder-led software companies with 2 to 20 engineers that need senior
        technical leadership but aren't ready for a full-time CTO or VP of Engineering.
      </p>
      <p class="read-more"><a href="/consulting">See how I can help &rarr;</a></p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p>
        I also build small products at <a href="https://faebriel.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >Faebriel</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter showHobbies />
</Layout>
